      "title": "Google Maps satellite: owner-supplied local reference",
      "url": "https://www.google.com/maps/@13.6461969,123.2337541,80m/data=!3m1!1e3",
      "note": "Inspected owner-supplied ateneo-pacol.png on 2026-10-08; capture date unknown. URL locates the site. Broad northern multi-crown belt and west/south groves, distinguishable crowns in field and drive rows, basketball-edge trees, parking-edge trees, courtyard garden islands, small low green frontage strips and southern courtyard lawn. Northern canopy follows the mapped campus edge and excludes the river/external grove. The western mottled field includes dry grass; the distinct reddish worn patch south of its crown row remains bare soil. Main mapped drive/roofs remain complete. No invented lamps, seats or species. Crown-width observations: North belt: roughly 80-100 px crowns; southwest grove 70-95 px; distinguishable drive/court rows 30-50 px. Large courtyard roof, gym and southern grade-school block all visible. Complete mapped courtyard hole is preserved. Independent excluded check errors: 4.12 m, 3.75 m. Visible crown centers are fitted to clear trunks within the observed crown footprint (maximum seven metres); crowns may overhang roofs and roads. Crown widths in the dense belts are estimated from image pixels against their matched local roof scale; existing circular crowns approximate irregular/elliptical image crowns. Complete mapped roofs, pitches, full-width paths/roads, water and farmland remain unchanged. Planted islands take precedence over exposed paving; ground under opaque canopy is not invented. No surveyed boundary, species, construction date or exact inventory inferred; no bitmap ships. Owner grass correction (2026-10-08): The western open field has continuous mottled low turf, including tan/dry grass and worn patches. Color alone did not establish bare soil. Add the exposed dry field and small fringes, preserving the distinct reddish bare patch south of the tree row, court, parking and drives. Flat south-courtyard green strips are grass; retain the shaped northern courtyard beds and dense frontage planting/shrubs. Classification uses texture, form and context, including dry turf, rather than green hue alone. Added ground excludes opaque observed crowns; original tree positions, routes and registration remain unchanged."
